== part 2: sloppy quorum, N=3, W=2, R=2 (R+W>N)
   home replicas of key k: A, B, C; the next node on the ring is D
   t=1  writer can reach A and D only (B, C unreachable from the writer)
   t=1  write k=v2 -> A: stored v2
   t=1  write k=v2 -> D: stored v2 with hint 'belongs to B' (hinted handoff)
   t=1  W=2 acknowledgements (A, D): write ACKNOWLEDGED
   t=2  reader can reach B and C only
   t=2  read k <- B: v1; read k <- C: v1; R=2 replies: returns v1
   result: STALE read although R+W>N: the write quorum {A,D} and the read quorum {B,C}
           do not intersect, because D is not one of the key's home replicas
   t=9  partition heals; D hands v2 over to B and deletes its hinted copy
